# sof-discord-bot — system overview
# A trigger subscriber: the game fires an event, the bot reads the snapshot
# the game wrote, draws a scoreboard, posts it to a Discord webhook.
# Zones run left to right: entry points -> core -> state -> external.
# Style classes set strokes only, so light and dark stay readable.

title: |md
  # sof-discord-bot
  A Discord webhook bot for Soldier of Fortune 1 servers: it subscribes to `sof-export-fire` events, reads the info snapshot the game just wrote, renders a scoreboard image, and posts it.
| {near: top-center}

direction: right
grid-columns: 2
grid-rows: 2
horizontal-gap: 140
vertical-gap: 140

entry: Entry points {
  direction: down

  cli: `sof-discord-bot` · console script → `cli.main` → `run_watcher`, one blocking loop
  addon: `sofplus/addons/info_client.func` · snapshots server and players into cvars, then fires `discord`
  trig: `sofplus/addons/ext_trigger.func` · vendored trigger helper: one file write per event
  timer: `sofplus/addons/sp_sc_timer_2.func` · vendored timer helper the snapshots run on
  svc: `systemd/` · bot unit plus the export-fire unit it depends on
}

core: Core {
  direction: down

  sub: `trigger_client.subscribe_forever` · JSON lines: hello, subscribe, ping· reconnect with backoff
  handler: `DiscordTriggerHandler.handle_trigger` · per-event domain logic · skip when no active players
  reader: `exporter.read_data_from_sof_server` · server.cfg + player files + the trigger file
  parse: `set "k" "v"` regex · strips `_sp_sv_info_` and `~discord_` prefixes, coerce ints
  board: `scoreboard.generate_screenshot_for_port` · PIL composite: map, portraits, text, flags
  post: `discorder.generate_payload` / `send_to_discord` · embed plus PNG, `?wait=true`, URL masked in logs
  log: `logging_utils` · one format, level from `SOF_BOT_LOG`
  fake: `fakedata.py` · sample players for developers, imported by nothing

  sub -> handler: one dict per event
  handler -> reader: what port, which data dir
  reader -> parse: raw cfg files in
  handler -> board: players in, PNG out
  board -> post: image plus embed
}

state: State {
  direction: down

  env: `.env` / systemd `EnvironmentFile` · webhooks, host, port, log level {shape: cylinder}
  data: `user-<port>/sofplus/data/` · `info_server`, `info_client(_snap)`, `ext_trigger` {shape: cylinder}
  assets: `src/.../assets/` · conchars, flags, optional map screenshots {shape: cylinder}
  paks: `base/pak0.pak`, `pak2.pak` · portraits and conchars, cached per process {shape: cylinder}
  seq: `_last_seq` per port · in memory only, used to warn on restarts {shape: cylinder}
}

ext: External {
  direction: down

  fire: `sof-export-fire` on 127.0.0.1:8765 · separate install, owns watching and dedupe
  discord: Discord webhook API · embed JSON, then multipart PNG
  sof: SoF server plus SoFplus · writes every file this bot reads
  paklib: vendored `pak.py`, `m32lib.py` · PAK index and M32 mip decoding
}

entry -> core: the game fires, the bot wakes
core -> state
core -> ext: subscribe in, webhook out

classes: {
  entry: {style: {stroke: "#2f6fbf"}}
  core: {style: {stroke: "#2f8f5f"}}
  state: {style: {stroke: "#a86a12"; stroke-dash: 3}}
  ext: {style: {stroke: "#8a4fbf"; stroke-dash: 5}}
}

entry.class: entry
core.class: core
state.class: state
ext.class: ext
